What is a growth mindset? how does it differ from a fixed mindset? So a fixed mindset is the belief that intellectual ability is just fixed. You have a certain amount of it and that's it. That's who you are and that's who you'll stay. That mindset can make challenges and mistakes more threatening because they can reveal deficiencies in your permanent ability. A growth mindset is the belief that students can develop their intellectual abilities
