American teenagers, in a very large study we did, overwhelmingly chose the easy problems, not the hard problems, in the control group. And that's interesting because when I was a teacher, I spent all my time coming up with really demanding and rigorous learning opportunities. I wanted to have that challenging, you know, stand-and-deliver type curriculum. And yet, many of my students might shy away from that. And in fact, we find nationally many students shy away from that. What happened in the treatment group when students got the growth mindset?
在我们做的一项规模非常大的研究中，美国青少年在对照组中绝大多数都选择了简单的题目，而不是困难的题目。这很有趣，因为当我是一名教师时，我把所有的精力都花在了想出真正要求严格、严谨的学习机会上。我希望拥有那种具有挑战性的、你知道的“站着讲课”类型的课程。然而，我的许多学生却可能会对此退缩。事实上，我们发现全国范围内有许多学生对此退缩。当学生获得成长型思维时，实验组会发生什么？

